# Redoubt drm-permission-default.patch (Android, LW-M7-39): DRM off by default,
# with Fenix's own Settings entry as the switch that turns it on.
#
# STATUS 2026-10-14: PENDING -- on disk, in NO patch list (PATCH-SCOPE.md,
# "Pending"). Do not list it on Firefox 158. It needs the settings half
# (android.cfg without media.eme.enabled=false), and with media.eme.enabled
# true, any page that calls navigator.requestMediaKeySystemAccess() for
# Widevine crashes the content process on Android 12+, where 158.0-2 isolates
# it. Gecko checks key-system support (MediaDrmProxy.isSchemeSupported ->
# MediaDrm.isCryptoSchemeSupported) in the content process BEFORE the app is
# asked. In an isolated_app process SELinux denies the DRM HAL lookup, the call
# throws IllegalArgumentException("Failed to query crypto scheme support") on
# the Gecko thread, the tab crashes, Fenix reloads it, and it crashes again (a
# crash loop, whatever the DRM setting says). Measured on the API 34 emulator
# with this patch and that cfg change: 836 such content crashes in about 7
# minutes of EME probes (docs/android/evidence/lw-m7-51/). The isolation study
# (docs/android/ISOLATION-MEDIA-STUDY.md) lists upstream bugs 2067689 and
# 2075686, FIXED in Firefox 159, as the EME work on this path; whether they
# cover this crash is to be measured on 159. Below Android 12 (no isolation,
# API 30 emulator) the design works as intended: default Blocked rejects,
# Allowed resolves Widevine, Ask to allow shows the DRM prompt, no crash.
# Re-test on the 159 rebase, or choose an SDK-gated variant (owner decision).
#
# Upstream files touched
# -----------------------
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/PhoneFeature.kt
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/sitepermissions/SitePermissionsManagePhoneFeatureFragment.kt
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/Settings.kt
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/PhoneFeatureTest.kt
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/SettingsTest.kt
#
# Line numbers are from the Firefox 158.0 tree AFTER the patches listed before
# this one in assets/patches/android.txt.
#
# Why
# ---
# LibreWolf desktop ships DRM off but unlocked (policies.json
# EncryptedMediaExtensions {"Enabled": false} -> default-branch
# media.eme.enabled=false; the "Play DRM-controlled content" checkbox in
# Settings turns it on). Until this patch, Redoubt's android.cfg set the same
# defaultPref (LW-M3-06). On Android that pref has no UI: Gecko rejects every
# key system on it (dom/media/eme/MediaKeySystemAccessManager.cpp
# RequestMediaKeySystemAccess, "EME has been preffed off"; with LibreWolf's
# eme-permission-common.patch this includes Clear Key) BEFORE the app is asked,
# so Fenix's Settings > Site settings > DRM-controlled content could never
# turn DRM on. The only way was about:config.
#
# What it does
# ------------
# GeckoView already sets media.eme.require-app-approval
# (mobile/android/app/geckoview-prefs.js), so after Gecko has checked that the
# key system and configuration are supported it asks the app
# (CheckDoesAppAllowProtectedMedia -> GeckoViewPermission ->
# PERMISSION_MEDIA_KEY_SYSTEM_ACCESS -> SitePermissionsFeature). This patch
# makes that permission's default Blocked instead of Ask to allow:
#   * PhoneFeature.getDefault(): MEDIA_KEY_SYSTEM_ACCESS -> BLOCKED. Every
#     reader of the setting (the Site settings screen, its summary,
#     PhoneFeature.getStatus) goes through getAction(), which passes this
#     default.
#   * Settings.getSitePermissionsCustomSettingsRules(): mediaKeySystemAccess is
#     read through PhoneFeature.getAction() instead of the hard-coded
#     ASK_TO_ALLOW default, so the rules SitePermissionsFeature applies and
#     the screen agree.
#   * SitePermissionsManagePhoneFeatureFragment: on the DRM-controlled content
#     screen, the "Recommended" tag moves from "Ask to allow" to "Blocked", so
#     the screen does not recommend something other than the default.
# With BLOCKED, SitePermissionsFeature.handleRuledFlow rejects the request
# without a prompt and shows the blocked-permission indicator; the page's
# requestMediaKeySystemAccess() rejects with NotSupportedError. Choosing "Ask
# to allow" or "Allowed" in Settings > Site settings > DRM-controlled
# content (Fenix's three-way choice) turns DRM on, globally or per site
# through the existing exceptions screen. A stored choice is kept: only the
# default for a profile that never chose changes.
#
# The settings-submodule half (LW-M7-39; written on the local Redoubt-settings
# branch android-drm-permission, bddc198f, not pushed, not in main's gitlink)
# drops android.cfg's defaultPref("media.eme.enabled", false), so Gecko's
# Android default (true, StaticPrefList.yaml) applies and the app permission
# is the only switch. Desktop is unchanged: its media.eme.enabled=false is in
# desktop.cfg.
#
# Tests: PhoneFeatureTest (default Blocked, stored choice kept);
# SettingsTest's default-rules fixture now has mediaKeySystemAccess = BLOCKED,
# and a new case checks the default and that "Ask to allow" is honoured.
#
# Ordering, for when it is listed: last in android.txt, on top of the seven
# patches that edit Settings.kt and the three that edit SettingsTest.kt; every
# pair measured order-free on 158.0 by swapping
# (docs/android/evidence/lw-m7-51/ordering-swap.py). Listing it needs those
# pairs in scripts/check-patch-order.py (the measured rows are in the
# evidence README) and a re-measure on the new tree.
#
diff --git a/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/PhoneFeature.kt b/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/PhoneFeature.kt
index 1954186..cf69468 100644
--- a/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/PhoneFeature.kt
+++ b/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/PhoneFeature.kt
@@ -167,6 +167,11 @@ enum class PhoneFeature(val androidPermissionsList: Array<String>) : Parcelable
         return when (this) {
             AUTOPLAY_AUDIBLE -> SitePermissionsRules.Action.BLOCKED
             AUTOPLAY_INAUDIBLE -> SitePermissionsRules.Action.ALLOWED
+            // Redoubt (LW-M7-39): DRM is off by default, as in LibreWolf (EncryptedMediaExtensions
+            // policy). GeckoView asks the app before any key system is used
+            // (media.eme.require-app-approval), so Blocked denies every site without a prompt,
+            // and Settings > Site settings > DRM-controlled content turns it on.
+            MEDIA_KEY_SYSTEM_ACCESS -> SitePermissionsRules.Action.BLOCKED
             else -> SitePermissionsRules.Action.ASK_TO_ALLOW
         }
     }
